{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 170,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where did quantum theory come from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2620,
    "dDurationMs": 4409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It started, not as a crazy idea, but with\na light bulb."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7029,
    "dDurationMs": 5650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the early 1890s, the German Bureau of Standards\nasked Max Planck how to make light bulbs more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12679,
    "dDurationMs": 4701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "efficient so that they would give out the\nmaximum light for the least electrical power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17380,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first task Planck faced was to predict\nhow much light a hot filament gives off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22270,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He knew that light consists of electromagnetic\nwaves, with different colors of light carried"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by different frequency waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28800,
    "dDurationMs": 4759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem was to ensure that as much light\nas possible was given off by visible waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33559,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than ultraviolet or infrared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36109,
    "dDurationMs": 5101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He tried to work out how much light of each\ncolor a hot object emits, but his predictions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41210,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "based on electromagnetic theory kept disagreeing\nwith experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45510,
    "dDurationMs": 5529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, in what he later called an “act\nof despair,” he threw the existing theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51039,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out the window and worked backwards from experimental\nmeasurements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54769,
    "dDurationMs": 7820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The data pointed him to a new rule of physics:\nlight waves carry energy only in packets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62589,
    "dDurationMs": 5051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with high frequency light consisting of large\npackets of energy and low frequency light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67640,
    "dDurationMs": 2649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consisting of small packets of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70289,
    "dDurationMs": 6741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea that light comes in packets, or \"quanta\",\nmay sound crazy, and it was at the time, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77030,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein soon related it to a much more familiar\nproblem: sharing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82670,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to make a kid happy... give them\na cookie!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86350,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if there are two kids, and you only have\none cookie, you'll only be able to cheer them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91140,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up half as much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93000,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if there are four, or eight, or sixteen\nhundred thousand, you're not going to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97590,
    "dDurationMs": 4069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them very happy at all if they have to share\none cookie between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101659,
    "dDurationMs": 5791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, if you have a room with infinitely\nmany kids but not infinitely many cookies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107450,
    "dDurationMs": 6479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you share the cookies evenly each kid will\nonly get an infinitesimally small crumb, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113929,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "none of them will be cheered up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115859,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they'll still eat all your cookies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118359,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The difference between light waves and kids\nis that you can't actually have infinitely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122979,
    "dDurationMs": 1611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many kids in a room."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124590,
    "dDurationMs": 5630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because light waves come in all sizes,\nyou can have arbitrarily small light waves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130220,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you can fit infinitely many into a room."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133760,
    "dDurationMs": 2839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the light waves would consume all\nyour cookies…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136599,
    "dDurationMs": 1561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138160,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, all these infinitesimal waves together\nwould have an infinite capacity to absorb"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143940,
    "dDurationMs": 5230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy, and they'd suck all the heat out of\nanything you put into the room… instantly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149170,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freezing the tea in your cup, or the sun,\nor even a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154110,
    "dDurationMs": 6050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Luckily, the universe doesn't work that way…\nbecause, as Planck guessed, the tiny, high"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160160,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frequency waves can only carry away energy\nin huge packets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164050,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're like fussy kids who'll only accept\nexactly thirty-seven cookies, or a hundred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169610,
    "dDurationMs": 4689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sixty-two thousand cookies, no more and\nno less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174299,
    "dDurationMs": 5461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because they're so picky, the fussy high frequency\nwaves lose out and most of the energy is carried"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179760,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away in lower-frequency packets that are willing\nto take an equal share."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184300,
    "dDurationMs": 7549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This common, average energy that the packets\ncarry, is in fact what we mean by \"temperature.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191849,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a higher temperature just means higher\naverage energy, and thus by Planck's rule,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196799,
    "dDurationMs": 2841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a higher frequency of light emitted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199640,
    "dDurationMs": 7159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why as an object gets hotter it glows\nfirst infrared, then red, yellow, white; hotter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206799,
    "dDurationMs": 5101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hotter towards blue, violet, ultraviolet…\nand so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211900,
    "dDurationMs": 5509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, Planck's quantum theory of fussy\nlight tells us that light bulb filaments should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217409,
    "dDurationMs": 6231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be heated to a temperature of about 3200 Kelvin\nto ensure that most of the energy is emitted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223640,
    "dDurationMs": 6010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as visible waves - much hotter, and we'd start\ntanning from the ultraviolet light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229650,
    "dDurationMs": 4929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, quantum physics has been staring\nus in the face since long before lightbulbs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234579,
    "dDurationMs": 6410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tanning beds: human beings have been making\nfires for millennia, with the color of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240989,
    "dDurationMs": 3691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flames spelling out \"quantum\" all along."
    } ]
  } ]
}
